# SEO (HTML + public)

Each real page must be crawlable without JavaScript.

## Required on every entry HTML

- Unique `<title>` (primary keyword + name, ~50–60 chars)
- Unique `meta name="description"` (~140–160 chars)
- `link rel="canonical"` to the live URL (`https://akashnalawade.com/…`)
- Open Graph + Twitter: `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:url`, `og:image`, `og:type`, `twitter:card`
- `html` language: `en` (add `lang="mr"` on Marathi nodes in React)

```html
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<link rel="canonical" href="https://akashnalawade.com/work/" />
<meta property="og:url" content="https://akashnalawade.com/work/" />

<!-- ❌ BAD: same title/description on every page, no canonical -->
```

## Site-wide files (`public/`)

- `robots.txt` allowing `/` and pointing to `sitemap.xml`
- `sitemap.xml` listing `/`, `/about/`, `/work/`
- JSON-LD `Person` (and `WebSite`) on the home HTML

Do not rely on client-only meta tags — crawlers on shared hosting read the static HTML.
